  "ethos:attribution": "Solar resource data (c) 2016 Solargis. Climate data (c) 2016 Solargis. Data obtained from the Global Solar Atlas 1.0 (http://globalsolaratlas.info), published by The World Bank Group; produced by Solargis. Published under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 IGO licence.",
  "ethos:license_status": "resolved",
  "ethos:coverage_note": "Holds seven of the layers of the January 2017 world download -- GHI, DNI, DIF, GTI (irradiation on an optimally tilted surface), PVOUT, TEMP and ELE -- each as a GeoTIFF with its .tfw world file, PDF poster map and ISO 19139 .xml metadata, plus the download's info.txt. The grid is 30 arcsec (about 1 km) over longitudes 180W-180E and latitudes 55S-60N: nothing north of 60N (most of Scandinavia, Iceland, Greenland, northern Russia and Canada) and nothing south of 55S (Antarctica). GHI, DNI, DIF, GTI and PVOUT are long-term averages of daily totals over 1994/1999/2007 (depending on the region) to 2015; TEMP covers 1994-2015; ELE is static. Values are daily averages, not annual sums.\nNot held: the optimum-tilt angle layer (OPTA), which info.txt lists but this copy lacks; monthly values; and the country and regional maps and layers the site offered beside the world files.",
  "ethos:retrieved": "2017-06-09",
  "ethos:origin": "downloaded",
